  "description": {
    "raw": "A flame, equivalent in brightness to a torch, springs forth from an object that you touch. The effect looks like a regular flame, but it creates no heat and doesn't use oxygen. A continual flame can be covered and hidden but not smothered or quenched.\n\nLight spells counter and dispel darkness spells of an equal or lower level.",
